    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_identity",
      "statement": "Correct objects, chemical bookkeeping and valid evidence.",
      "expected": "Inspect species_registry, every input/geometry mapping and real raw log. Verify stoichiometry, charge/multiplicity, method/state, stationarity or constrained label, and consistent thermochemistry. Use all four mapped heptazines and source substrate1a: N-methyl-N-(4-trifluoromethylphenyl)pivalamide. Pilot dFHeptZ/dOMeHeptZ first, then expand the same endpoint contract to dClHeptZ/dMeHeptZ. Use MeCN, 273.15 K, substrate0.1M, O2 1atm, 456nm source conditions; solute free energies use1M. Include substrate radical cation (charge+1,doublet), catalyst radical anion (−1,doublet), O2 triplet ground state, singlet oxygen and superoxide (−1,doublet). SET compares S+PC*→S+radical+PC−radical. EnT compares catalyst triplet deactivation with triplet-O2→singlet-O2; E00 and triplet gaps are not vertical S1 energies. A shared SCE reference may be used, but direct reaction G avoids arbitrary absolute-electrode shifts.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "source_1",
        "source_2",
        "upgrade_design"
      ]
    },
    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_photoredox_matrix",
      "statement": "Four catalysts on a common SET/EnT and redox/state reference.",
      "expected": "Four catalysts on a common SET/EnT and redox/state reference. Recompute quantities from identified raw jobs and evidence files. Check all required named matrix cells; prose or a legacy scalar cannot replace this endpoint. A scientific ambiguity is valid only after the relevant controls exist. Non-saddle/collapse alternatives require actual profiles and both endpoints, not failed optimization. A same-basin comparison may omit nonexistent independent numeric operands only after separate complete searches, mapped identity and stationarity demonstrate collapse; this never excuses a missing control. New numerical reference and tolerances are pending; never choose a preferred value or broaden a legacy tolerance to excuse wrong identity.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "source_1",
        "source_2",
        "upgrade_design"
      ]
    },
